# Template. Copy to secrets/<tool>.env (gitignored) and chmod 600:
#   cp secrets/opencode.env.example secrets/opencode.env && chmod 600 secrets/opencode.env
#
# Secrets for opencode's VM only. umbra loads this file into that VM's
# environment and nowhere else (not claude's, not agy's, not your shell's).
# Must stay mode 600. One KEY=VALUE per line; # starts a comment.
#
# github MCP (run it with --read-only in the sandbox's opencode config). Create a fine-grained token:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#     Token name:          umbra-opencode-readonly
#     Expiration:          90 days (or less)
#     Repository access:   Only select repositories  -> pick the ones the agent may read
#     Repository permissions (Read-only each):
#       Contents, Issues, Pull requests, Actions (optional), Metadata (auto)
#     Account permissions: none
# Then uncomment the next line and paste the token after the '=':
# GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN=github_pat_
